@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 160
hide footbox
title TechZone — purchase receipt and atomic stock increase
actor "ADMIN / PURCHASE" as Staff
boundary "React client" as UI
control "Express route\n+ auth guards" as API
control "purchases/service.js" as Purchase
control "inventory/service.js" as Stock
database "MongoDB\nreplica set" as DB
Staff -> UI : Submit received quantities
UI -> API : POST /api/purchases/\n:id/receipts\nitems, key, cookie
API -> DB : Resolve session\nand active user
DB --> API : User + role
API -> API : Check permission
API -> Purchase : receivePurchase(id,\nbody, userId, key)
Purchase -> Purchase : Normalize input; fingerprint\npurchase, actor and items
note over API, Purchase
  Invalid session / permission / input returns 401 / 403 / 400.
end note
group MongoDB transaction
  Purchase -> DB : Recheck actor; find\nreceipt by requestId
  DB --> Purchase : Existing receipt or none
  alt Existing key with different fingerprint
    Purchase -> Purchase : Reject with 409
  else Existing key with matching fingerprint
    Purchase -> DB : Read current purchase\n(no stock writes)
  else New key
    Purchase -> DB : Lock purchase\n(increment version)
    Purchase -> Purchase : Require ORDERED / PARTIAL;\nvalidate remaining quantities
    Purchase -> DB : Save receivedQty and\nPARTIAL / RECEIVED status
    loop Each received line
      Purchase -> Stock : applyStockChange\n(+qty, PURCHASE, purchaseId,\nuserId, session)
      Stock -> DB : Recheck actor;\nlock active product
      Stock -> DB : Guarded stock increase;\nappend inventory event
      Stock --> Purchase : Inventory event ID
    end
    Purchase -> DB : Create receipt with\nitems and event IDs
  end
  note over Purchase, DB
    Commit only on success. Any failure aborts the whole transaction,
    including order progress, all stock/history writes and the receipt.
  end note
end
Purchase --> API : Receipt + purchase or error
API --> UI : 201 {receipt, purchase}\nor error
UI --> Staff : Show result; refresh\ninventory after success
note over Purchase, DB
  Unique requestId prevents a second committed receipt for the same key.
  Duplicate-key recovery reauthorizes and validates the fingerprint.
  Replay returns the original receipt plus the current purchase.
end note
@enduml
